window.MONSTER_CHUNK_67 = [{"name":"Giant Squid","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +9 natural, -2 size","hp":102,"hd":"12d8+48","hdvalue":12,"fort":14,"ref":13,"will":5,"defensive_abilities":["ink cloud (20-ft. radius)"],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"speed_mod":"jet 260 ft.","melee":"bite +14 (2d6+7), 2 arms +14 (1d6+7), tentacles +12 (4d6+3/19-20 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft. (30 ft. with arms and tentacles)","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"4d6+10"}],"strength":25,"dexterity":17,"constitution":19,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":9,"cmb":18,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (tentacle)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"environments":["any oceans"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Immense in size, this great squid's tentacles writhe and flash with almost nauseating speed. The beast's eyes are as big as shields.","group":"Squid","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","description":"The giant squid is a legendary beast capable of feeding on humans with ease. Hunger has been known to drive these normally deep dwelling creatures up to the ocean surface where anything they encounter is potential prey. A giant squid is 45 ft. long and weighs 1,500 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Glass Urchin","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"vermin","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":-4,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"30 ft."}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":4,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"-4 Dex, +18 natural, -2 size","hp":126,"hd":"12d8+72","hdvalue":12,"fort":14,"ref":0,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["stability","transparency"],"immunities":["mindaffecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5}],"melee":"3 spines +17 (1d8+10 plus poison)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"poison spray"},{"type":"spines"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":3,"constitution":22,"wisdom":15,"charisma":2,"baseatk":9,"cmb":21,"cmd":27,"cmd_special":"+8 vs. bull rush or trip","skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":6}],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["warm coastlines","warm oceans"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cluster (3-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This strange-looking creature has a spherical body covered with hundreds or thousands of two-foot-long bright purple spines that darken to ominous black tips.","group":"Giant","source":"AP 37","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Glass urchin venom causes the senses to become clouded and creates vivid hallucinations and confusion in the victim's mind. The save DC is Constitution-based. Spines-contact or injury; save Fort DC 16; frequency 1/ round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Wis and confused for 1 round; cure 2 consecutive saves."},{"type":"Poison Spray","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, once every 5 rounds, a spear urchin can spray poison from numerous smaller spines across its body. This poison fills a 20-foot-radius spread around the urchin- all creatures within this area are exposed to the urchin's venom and must make Fortitude saves as detailed above to resist Wisdom damage and confusion. This attack is even more effective underwater, as the poison spray creates a cloud that lingers in the area around the urchin for 5 rounds-creatures must save each round they begin a turn in the area of the poison cloud in addition to when the urchin creates the effect."},{"type":"Spines","kind":"Ex","details":"A glass urchin's spines can swivel and rotate to face any approaching creature that attacks it. Any creature that attacks a glass urchin with an unarmed strike or a natural attack, or any Huge or smaller creature that attacks with a one-handed weapon or light weapon, is automatically attacked by the glass urchin's spines as an immediate action. If the spines hit, they can poison the target as well."},{"type":"Transparency","kind":"Ex","details":"A glass urchin's spines and body are transparent when underwater, granting the creature concealment and a constant 20% miss chance."}],"description":"Much more dangerous than their smaller kin, giant sea urchins are dangerous predators of opportunity. With the exception of the hunter urchin, giant sea urchins lie in wait for food to come to them, typically carried within reach of their attacks via ocean currents or, more commonly, tides. Hunter Urchins: These urchins can adjust their spines to effect an awkward method of locomotion on land. They actively seek prey, and possess long, rasp-like tongues that can whip out and pull food to them. Spear Urchins: These brightly colored creatures can fire spines like javelins, relying upon poison to slow down prey or eventually immobilize it so they can crawl over to feed. Glass Urchins: So named for their transparency, these beautiful creatures shimmer like delicate crystals. Yet for all the damage their spines can inf lict, victims of glass urchins generally do more damage to themselves or their allies due to the potent hallucinatory effects of this urchin's venom. Sea Urchins as Difficult Terrain The giant sea urchins presented here are fantastic evolutions of their much more common, smaller, and less offensive kin. Yet even the smaller common urchins can pose a problem for unwary adventurers. Sea urchins live in vast colonies on tidal rocks, and moving across a field of urchins can be quite awkward and painful. Their thousands of spines are just as sharp as those possessed by their larger kin, and they function as caltrops to anyone that walks over them. Worse, these spines are venomous, and can poison those who take damage from them. Those who succumb to the poison suffer searing pain that can sicken them for several minutes. Though uncomfortable, fortunately this venom doesn't actually inf lict either ability damage or ability drain. Sea Urchin Venom: Spines-injury; save Fort 11; frequency 1/minute for 6 minutes; effect victim is sickened for 1 minute; cure 1 save.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Air Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":14,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+10 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":18,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["air mastery"],"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +21 (2d8+7)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"whirlwind","details":"DC 23"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":31,"constitution":18,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":22,"cmd":43,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":25},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":23},{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15}],"languages":["Auran"],"environments":["any (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This cloud-like creature has dark hollows reminiscent of eyes and a mouth, and a howling wind whips it into ominous shapes.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against an air elemental."}],"description":"Air elementals are fast, flying creatures made of living air. Primitive and territorial, they resent being summoned or doing the bidding of mortals, and much prefer to spend their time on the Plane of Air, swooping and racing through the endless skies. Although all air elementals of a similar size have identical statistics, the exact appearance of an air elemental can vary wildly between individuals. One might be an animated vortex of wind and smoke, while another might be a smoky bird-like creature with glowing eyes and wind for wings. An air elemental prefers to attack flying or otherwise airbone targets, not only because its mastery over flight gives it a slight advantage, but also because it detests the thought of having to touch the ground. An air elemental can move underwater, and although it is an elemental and thus runs no risk of drowning, it has no ranks in Swim and loses much of its speed and mobility when underwater. Whirlwind Whirlwind Elemental Height Weight Save DC Height Small 4 ft. 1 lb. 12 10-20 ft. Medium 8 ft. 2 lbs. 14 10-30 ft. Large 16 ft. 4 lbs. 18 10-40 ft. Huge 32 ft. 8 lbs. 22 10-50 ft. Greater 36 ft. 10 lbs. 23 10-60 ft. Elder 40 ft. 12 lbs. 27 10-60 ft.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Earth Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +14 natural, -2 size","hp":136,"hd":"13d10+65","hdvalue":13,"fort":13,"ref":3,"will":8,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":20}],"speed_mod":"earth glide","melee":"2 slams +21 (2d10+10)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"earth mastery"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":8,"constitution":21,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":25,"cmd":34,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":10},{"skill":"Climb","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7}],"languages":["Terran"],"environments":["any (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This hulking, roughly humanoid creature of dirt and stone explodes up from the earth, faceless save for two glowing gemstone eyes.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Earth Glide","kind":"Ex","details":"A burrowing earth elemental can pass through stone, dirt, or almost any other sort of earth except metal as easily as a fish swims through water. If protected against fire damage, it can even glide through lava. Its burrowing leaves behind no tunnel or hole, nor does it create any ripple or other sign of its presence. A move earth spell cast on an area containing a burrowing earth elemental flings the elemental back 30 ft., stunning the creature for 1 round unless it succeeds on a DC 15 Fortitude save."},{"type":"Earth Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"An earth elemental gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its foe are touching the ground. If an opponent is airborne or waterborne, the elemental takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls. These modifiers apply to bull rush and overrun maneuvers, whether the elemental is initiating or resisting these kinds of attacks. (These modifiers are not included in the statistics block.)"}],"description":"Earth elementals are plodding, stubborn creatures made of living stone or earth. When utterly still, they resemble a heap of stone or a small hill. When an earth elemental lumbers into action, its actual appearance can vary, although its statistics remain identical to other elementals of its size. Most earth elementals look like terrestrial animals made out of rock, earth, or even crystal, with glowing gemstones for eyes. Larger earth elementals often have a stony humanoid appearance. Bits of vegetation frequently grow in the soil that makes up parts of an earth elemental's body. Elemental Height Weight Small 4 ft. 80 lbs. Medium 8 ft. 750 lbs. Large 16 ft. 6,000 lbs. Huge 32 ft. 48,000 lbs. Greater 36 ft. 54,000 lbs. Elder 40 ft. 60,000 lbs.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Fire Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":12,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":16,"will":6,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60}],"melee":"2 slams +19 (2d8+7 plus burn)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"2d8, DC 20"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":27,"constitution":18,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":22,"cmd":41,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Wind Stance"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":23},{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":16}],"languages":["Ignan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a living, mobile bonfire, tongues of flame reaching out in search of things to burn.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","description":"Fire elementals are quick, cruel creatures of living flame. They enjoy frightening beings weaker than themselves, and terrorizing any creature they can set on fire. A fire elemental cannot enter water or any other nonf lammable liquid. A body of water is an impassible barrier unless the fire elemental can step or jump over it or the water is covered with a flammable material (such as a layer of oil). Fire elementals vary in appearance-they usually manifest as coiling serpentine forms made of smoke and lame, but some fire elementals take on shapes more akin to humans, demons, or other monsters in order to increase the terror of their sudden appearance. Features on a fire elemental's body are made by darker bits of flame or patches of semi-stable smoke, ash, and cinders. Elemental Height Weight Small 4 ft. 1 lb. Medium 8 ft. 2 lbs. Large 16 ft. 4 lbs. Huge 32 ft. 8 lbs. Greater 36 ft. 10 lbs. Elder 40 ft. 12 lbs.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Ice Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","cold","elemental","extraplanar","water"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"snow vision"}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +1 dodge, +10 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":14,"will":4,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["cold","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":20,"special":"ice and snow only"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"2 slams +20 (2d8+9 plus 2d6 cold)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"numbing cold","details":"DC 20"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":18,"constitution":19,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":24,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Swim","value":17}],"languages":["Aquan"],"sq":[{"type":"ice glide"},{"type":"icewalking"}],"environments":["any land (Plane of Water)","any water (Plane of Water)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"From the waist up, this icy creature's features are humanoid, but below its body is a snake-like, slithering tail.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ice Glide","kind":"Su","details":"A burrowing ice elemental can pass through nonmagical ice and snow as easily as a fish swims through water. Its burrowing leaves behind no tunnel or hole, nor does it create any ripple or other sign of its presence. A control water spell cast on an area containing a burrowing ice elemental flings the elemental back 30 ft., stunning the creature for 1 round unless it succeeds on a DC 15 Fortitude save."},{"type":"Icewalking","kind":"Ex","details":"This ability works like the spider climb spell, but the surfaces the elemental climbs must be icy. The elemental can move across icy surfaces without penalty and doesn't need to make Acrobatics checks to run or charge on ice."},{"type":"Numbing Cold","kind":"Su","details":"When an ice elemental deals cold damage to a creature, that creature must succeed on a Fortitude save or be staggered for 1 round. The save DC is listed in the elemental's stat block and is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Snow Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"An ice elemental can see perfectly well in snowy conditions and doesn't take any penalties on Perception checks while in snow."}],"description":"Ice elementals are creatures made of animated snow and ice. They form in especially cold parts of the Plane of Water and along its border with the Plane of Air, where giant icebergs careen off of world-high waterfalls into the open sky. Ice elementals vary in their exact appearance.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Lightning Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":13,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+9 Dex, +1 dodge, +4 natural, -2 size","hp":110,"hd":"13d10+39","hdvalue":13,"fort":11,"ref":17,"will":6,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["electricity","elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +20 (2d8+6 plus 2d6 electricity)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"metal mastery"},{"type":"spark leap"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":29,"constitution":16,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":21,"cmd":41,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":25},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":25},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":16}],"languages":["Auran"],"environments":["any (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a dark storm cloud, with sparks suggesting eyes and long sweeping arms charged with bolts of lightning.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Metal Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"A lightning elemental gains a +3 bonus on attack rolls if its opponent is wearing metal armor, is wielding a metal weapon, or is made of metal (such as an iron golem)."},{"type":"Spark Leap","kind":"Ex","details":"A lightning elemental gains a +10 bonus on bull rush, disarm, overrun, and trip attacks when it charges a creature against whom its metal mastery ability applies."}],"description":"Though most think of the Plane of Air as a vast expanse of clear sky, that plane also holds the power of the storm, including monstrous hurricanes larger than entire worlds and thunderstorms whose peals and claps can shatter stone. Whether lightning elementals are the byproduct of common air elementals spending too much time near these electrically charged storms or are merely calved off like forgotten flurries, they are aggressive and almost suicidal in their willingness to leap into battle. They particularly enjoy attacking creatures that are made of metal and creatures that wear metal armor or wield metal weapons. Many lightning elementals have a roughly humanoid shape, but some prefer animalistic shapes (particularly birds and dragons), and a few appear to be nothing more than large disembodied heads made of dark clouds with flickering lightning tongues. Regardless of the shape a lightning elemental takes, the air around the creature hums and throbs with the promise of electrocution and the tangy stink of ozone.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Magma Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +12 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":7,"will":4,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["fire","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":20}],"speed_mod":"earth glide","melee":"2 slams +18 (2d8+7 plus burn)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"2d6, DC 18"},{"type":"lava puddle"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":8,"constitution":19,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":22,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":23},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7}],"languages":["Ignan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This rocky monster glows with an internal heat. Red light spills from its eyes and mouth, as well as fractures in its outer surface.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Burn","kind":"Ex","details":"A magma elemental's burn DC includes a -2 racial penalty, as their fires don't burn quite as hot as true elemental flames."},{"type":"Earth Glide","kind":"Ex","details":"A burrowing magma elemental can pass through stone, dirt, lava, or almost any other sort of earth except metal as easily as a fish swims through water. Its burrowing leaves behind no tunnel or hole, nor does it create any ripple, though the area it passes through feels warm for 1 round afterward and often retains a strangely smooth texture, as if the stone had been polished. A move earth spell cast on an area containing a burrowing magma elemental flings the elemental back 30 ft., stunning the creature for 1 round unless it succeeds on a DC 15 Fortitude save."},{"type":"Lava Puddle","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a full-round action, a magma elemental can vomit forth a puddle of lava that fills its space to a depth of 2-3 inches and counts as difficult terrain. Any creature that moves through this puddle of lava takes 2d6 points of fire damage. This damage continues for 1d3 rounds after the creature leaves the lava pool, although then it only inflicts 1d6 points of fire damage per round. The lava puddle solidifies and is safe to touch after a number of rounds equal to the elemental's Hit Dice. At the GM's discretion, this puddle of lava could start secondary fires."}],"description":"In the border areas between the Plane of Earth and Plane of Fire, volcanoes and continent-sized lava flows are commonplace. Elementals in this area tend to have aspects of both planes, and the typical sort is the magma elemental, an earth elemental with a core of liquid fire. Magma elementals generally have a somewhat feral or bestial appearance.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Mud Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","extraplanar","water"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"30 ft."}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":14,"will":4,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["acid","elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":10},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"speed_mod":"earth glide","melee":"2 slams +20 (2d8+9 plus entrap)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"entrap","details":"DC 20, 10 minutes, hardness 10, hp 15"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":18,"constitution":19,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":24,"cmd":39,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":25},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Swim","value":17}],"languages":["Terran"],"environments":["any land (Plane of Earth)","any water (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This animate pile of mud seems barely able to maintain the semblance of a humanoid form made of dripping sludge.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Earth Glide","kind":"Ex","details":"A burrowing mud elemental can pass through dirt, gravel, or other loose or porous solid matter as easily as a fish swims through water. It cannot use this ability to pass through a solid barrier such as a stone or brick wall. Its burrowing leaves behind no tunnel or hole, nor does it create any ripple or other sign of its presence. A move earth spell cast on an area containing a burrowing mud elemental flings the elemental back 30 ft., stunning the creature for 1 round unless it succeeds on a DC 15 Fortitude save."},{"type":"Entrap","kind":"Ex","details":"The mud from an elemental's entrap ability can be washed away in 1d3 rounds of immersion in water."}],"description":"Where the Plane of Earth borders the Plane of Water, a mixing of the fundamental elements occurs-it is in this borderland that the mud elementals dwell. Scorned by earth and water elementals, mud elementals usually look like vaguely recognizable blobs of mud in the shape of a Material Plane creature, whether a humanoid, an animal, or even an immense insect. The exact density of their muddy bodies varies-some might be composed of silty water, while others are thick, like river clay. Large and powerful mud elementals tend to have worm-like, reptilian, or frog-like forms.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Greater Water Elemental","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","water"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -2 size","hp":123,"hd":"13d10+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":15,"will":4,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":90}],"melee":"2 slams +20 (2d8+9)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"drench"},{"type":"vortex","details":"DC 25"},{"type":"water mastery"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":20,"constitution":19,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":13,"cmb":24,"cmd":40,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":18},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Swim","value":30}],"languages":["Aquan"],"environments":["any (Plane of Water)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This translucent creature's shape shifts between a spinning column of water and a crashing wave.","group":"Elemental","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Drench","kind":"Ex","details":"The elemental's touch puts out nonmagical flames of Large size or smaller. The creature can dispel magical fire it touches as dispel magic (caster level equals elemental's HD)."},{"type":"Vortex","kind":"Su","details":"A water elemental can create a whirlpool as a standard action, at will. This ability functions identically to the whirlwind special attack, but can only form underwater and cannot leave the water."},{"type":"Water Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"A water elemental gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its opponent are touching water. If the opponent or the elemental is touching the ground, the elemental takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls. These modifiers apply to bull rush and overrun maneuvers, whether the elemental is initiating or resisting these kinds of attacks."}],"description":"Water elementals are patient, relentless creatures made of living fresh or salt water. They prefer to hide or drag their opponents into the water to gain an advantage. As with other elementals, all water elementals have their own unique shapes and appearances. Most appear as wave-like creatures with vaguely humanoid faces and smaller wave \"arms\" to either side. Another common form is that of any aquatic creature, such as a shark or octopus, but made entirely out of water.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ijiraq","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"fey","subtypes":["shapechanger"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural","hp":105,"hd":"14d6+56","hdvalue":14,"fort":8,"ref":13,"will":13,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +10 (2d4+3), bite +10 (2d6+3), gore +10 (2d6+3)","ranged":"javelin +9 (1d6+3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"disorienting gaze"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"fly"},{"spell":"hallucinatory terrain"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"baleful polymorph"},{"spell":"control winds"},{"spell":"cure critical wounds"},{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"sleet storm"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally IV"}]}],"strength":16,"dexterity":15,"constitution":18,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":19,"charisma":22,"baseatk":7,"cmb":10,"cmd":23,"feats":[{"feat":"Acrobatic Steps"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Nimble Moves"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":19},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":21},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19},{"skill":"Survival","value":18}],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"elk, beast shape II"},{"type":"hide in plain sight"}],"environments":["cold forests","cold plains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard (mostly valuable scrimshaw carvings)","description_visual":"Its head the skull of a caribou, this humanoid has wicked claws, and wears wrappings of ragged fur adorned with scrimshaw talismans.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Disorienting Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"An ijiraq can level an icy stare at a creature within 30 ft. That creature takes a -20 penalty on Perception checks and Survival checks for 24 hours (Fortitude DC 23 negates). The save DC is Charisma-based. An ijiraq can use this ability while in the shape of an elk."},{"type":"Hide in Plain Sight","kind":"Su","details":"An ijiraq can use the Stealth skill even while being observed. As long as it's standing in terrain covered in ice or snow, an ijiraq can hide itself from view in the open without actually hiding behind anything. An ijiraq can't use this ability while flying, and the ability has no effect when the ijiraq isn't in icy terrain."}],"description":"Wardens of the north, ijiraqs protect the frigid beauty and placidity of their arctic homes against all who would trespass, regardless of race or intentions. They are creatures of icy resolution, merciless and unf linching as the arctic winds, bringing doom to both vicious and innocent interlopers equally. Aloof and mysterious, they prefer not to be seen in their natural form, instead cloaking themselves in the fur and shape of swift elk or caribou. Yet even then they're usually only glimpsed as fleeting shadows. Those who lock gazes with ijiraqs see the world around them begin to swim, seeming unreal to the extent that even a skilled forester might be unable to determine which way is north, and a life-long native of a place might become lost within sight of home. Few can honestly claim to have ever seen an ijiraq's true face, as the creatures wear skulls taken from impressive specimens of their alternate forms as masks. Ijiraqs typically stand about 5 ft. tall-though that height reaches over 6 ft. including their impressive horns- and weigh approximately 175 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Irnakurse","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"aberration","init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size","hp":105,"hd":"10d8+60","hdvalue":10,"fort":9,"ref":8,"will":9,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +8 14 (1d8+7), 4 tentacles +8 (1d6+3 plus mind lash)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with tentacles)","special_attacks":[{"type":"soul scream"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 tentacles 2d6+10; 3 tentacles 3d6+10; 4 tentacles 4d6+10"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":17,"constitution":23,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":14,"charisma":18,"baseatk":7,"cmb":15,"cmd":28,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deflect Arrows"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tentacle)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12}],"languages":["Elven (can't speak)"],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A mad-eyed mess of deformed limbs, misplaced features, and bone shards pulls itself along amid a cacophony of slapping flesh.","group":"Fleshwarp","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Mind Lash","kind":"Su","details":"Those struck by an irnakurse are overwhelmed with dark emotions and corrupted images of a ruined life. Any non-evil creature hit by an irnakurse's tentacle must succeed at a DC 19 Will save or be stunned for 1 round. A creature that successfully saves can't be affected by the same irnakurse's mind lash for 24 hours. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Soul Scream","kind":"Su","details":"Capable of channeling all of its rage and terror into a single, unnatural noise, an irnakurse can unleash a sound of alien horror as a standard action. Any non-evil creature within 30 ft. of a screaming irnakurse must succeed at a DC 19 Will save or take 1d4 points of Wisdom drain. Once it begins screaming, an irnakurse can continue as a free action for 6 rounds, but can't scream again for 5 minutes afterward. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Irnakurse, meaning \"perfect ones\" in the Elven language, represent the sum outpouring of drow hatred for their surface-world brethren. These brainwashed, rage-filled abominations are the result of elves subjected to fleshwarping-and were the drow to have their way, embodiments of the elven race's future. Each irnakurse suffers long under the knife of the dark elves' most practiced fleshwarpers until its body and mind lie in total ruin. When the weeks of torture and transformation are complete, what was once an elf emerges as a shrieking mockery of its lost grace, a horror of reworked flesh and broken bones, a \"perfect\" elf to the drow and a sin against life to elvenkind. Through the blasphemous tortures that create them, irnakurse are made completely mad and become unable to harm drow. All non-drow, however, they view as targets to vent their terror and rage upon. Elves especially provoke irnakurses' ire. No two irnakurse look exactly the same-drow torturers take profane pride in sculpting their elven victims into unique masterpieces of agony-most stand between 8 and 9 ft. tall and weigh upward of 300 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Juvenile Copper Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CG","size":"Medium","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +13 natural","hp":115,"hd":"11d12+44","hdvalue":11,"fort":11,"ref":9,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["uncanny dodge"],"immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":150,"maneuverability":"average"}],"speed_mod":"climb stone","melee":"bite +16 (1d8+7/19-20), 2 claws +16 (1d6+5/19-20), 2 wings +11 (1d4+2)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"60-ft. line, DC 19, 8d6 acid"},{"type":"slow breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"grease"},{"spell":"hideous laughter"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":3,"spellsknown_concentration":7,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"silent image"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":14,"constitution":19,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":11,"cmb":16,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. trip","cmd":28,"cmd_special":"+6 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":17},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":21},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":17},{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":17,"special":"+21 vs. traps"},{"skill":"Perform (comedy)","value":14},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":17}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Gnome","Halfling"],"sq":[{"type":"trap master"}],"environments":["warm hills"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Bright, shining copper scales run from the horn-crowned head to the ridged tail of this long-winged dragon.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Climb Stone","kind":"Ex","details":"A copper dragon can climb on stone surfaces as though using the spider climb spell."},{"type":"Slow Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of acid, a copper dragon can breathe a cone of slowing gas. Those in the cone must make a Fortitude save or be slowed (as per the spell slow) for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category of the dragon."},{"type":"Trap Master","kind":"Ex","details":"A juvenile or older copper dragon receives a +1 bonus per age category on Craft (traps) and Perception checks made to locate a trap. Upon becoming a mature adult, he can also use Disable Device to disarm magic traps as if he had the rogue's Trapfinding class feature."}],"description":"This whimsical dragon spends most of its time in combat trying to annoy and frustrate its enemies.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Juvenile Green Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (120 ft., DC 17)"],"ac":23,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +13 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d12+44","hdvalue":11,"fort":11,"ref":8,"will":11,"immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +16 (2d6+9/19-20), 2 claws +16 (1d8+6), 2 wings +11 (1d6+3), tail slap +11 (1d8+9)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, DC 19, 8d6 acid"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"entangle"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":5,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"summon monster I"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":12,"constitution":19,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":14,"baseatk":11,"cmb":18,"cmd":29,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":16},{"skill":"Swim","value":28}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"woodland stride"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Scales the color of emeralds armor this ferocious dragon. A single sharp horn protrudes from the end of its toothy snout.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A green dragon can breathe underwater indefinitely and can freely use its breath weapon, spells, and other abilities while submerged."},{"type":"Woodland Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older green dragon can move through any sort of foliage at full speed without taking damage or suffering impairment. Areas of foliage that have been magically manipulated affect it normally."}],"description":"Green dragons dwell in the ancient forests of the world, prowling under towering canopies in search of prey. Of all the chromatic dragons, green dragons are perhaps the easiest to deal with diplomatically.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Jyoti","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+4 armor, +5 Dex, +1 dodge, +4 natural","hp":104,"hd":"11d10+44","hdvalue":11,"hp_mods":["fast healing 10"],"fort":11,"ref":8,"will":11,"save_mods":"+2 vs. divine","defensive_abilities":["divine aversion","positive energy affinity"],"immunities":["death attacks","disease","energy drain","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10},{"type":"sonic","value":10}],"sr":20,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":90,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+1 ghost touch spear +14 (1d8+4/x3 plus 1d6 fire), bite +8 (1d6+1 plus 1d6 fire)","ranged":"ray +16 ranged touch (by spell)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"60-ft. cone, 11d6 fire, Reflex DC 19 half, usable once every 1d4 rounds"},{"type":"positive energy"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"mage armor"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"breath of life"},{"spell":"disrupting weapon"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"cure serious wounds"},{"spell":"daylight"},{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"lesser restoration"},{"spell":"searing light"}]}],"strength":14,"dexterity":20,"constitution":19,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":15,"baseatk":11,"cmb":13,"cmd":29,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Wind Stance"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Heal","value":16},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19}],"languages":["Aquan","Auran","Common","Ignan","Terran"],"environments":["any (Positive Energy Plane)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","flight (3-8)"],"treasure":"double (+1 ghost touch spear)","description_visual":"This phoenix-like humanoid is surrounded by a halo of radiant energy. Its spear is tipped with a carved crystal blade.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A jyoti's breath weapon is a focused burst of searing fire infused with positive energy. Undead in the area take 11d8 damage rather than 11d6."},{"type":"Divine Aversion","kind":"Su","details":"Jyoti dislike deities and are never divine spellcasters. Jyoti gain a +2 racial bonus on saves against divine magical effects."},{"type":"Positive Energy","kind":"Su","details":"A jyoti's natural weapons and any weapons it wields strike as if they were ghost touch weapons. In addition, any weapon (natural or manufactured) a jyoti uses deals +1d6 fire damage on a hit."},{"type":"Positive Energy Affinity","kind":"Ex","details":"A jyoti can exist comfortably on the Positive Energy Plane, and doesn't benefit (or suffer) from that plane's overwhelming infusions of life-giving energies. Whenever a jyoti is subjected to a magical healing effect, that effect functions at its full potential, as if enhanced by Maximize Spell."}],"description":"Enigmatic and swift to anger, the avian race known as the jyoti are xenophobic natives of the Positive Energy Plane. Though some believe the jyoti are inherently good because their home plane is the source of all life, these beliefs are quite in error, for the jyoti react to all other races with wary suspicion at best, and usually assume the worst and attack before they can themselves be attacked. They guard their crystalline cities from all intrusion, especially by creatures from other planes and servants of the gods. They have been known to hold dangerous artifacts in their vaults on behalf of desperate visitors, though in the case of holy or unholy artifacts, the jyoti are more likely to destroy the artifacts as soon as possible.\n\nJyoti loathe natives of the Shadow Plane and the Negative Energy Plane in particular, though there is an element of pity in their actions toward undead. They never discuss the sceaduinar, and even hearing that name inf lames jyoti into immediate anger. Those who dare argue on the sceaduinar's behalf are immediately attacked.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Kithangian","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"all-around vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+16 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d10+55","hdvalue":11,"fort":12,"ref":9,"will":7,"dr":"10/good","immunities":["electricity","fear","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":20,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"2 claws +16 (1d6+6/19-20 plus grab), 2 stings +16 (1d6+6/19-20 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"hatred"},{"type":"rasping tongues"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"speak with animals"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"},{"spell":"hold animal"},{"spell":"unnatural lust"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"baleful polymorph"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 3, 1 kithangian 35%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"air walk"},{"spell":"quickened unnatural lust"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":11,"constitution":20,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":19,"charisma":16,"baseatk":11,"cmb":18,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":28,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (sting)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (unnatural lust)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":17},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Draconic","speak with animals","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"beast shape II, Medium or Large animal"},{"type":"swift transformation"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (3-8)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature combines the features of a scorpion and a horse- slavering humanoid faces peer from between its two pincers.","group":"Demon","source":"The Worldwound","special_abilities":[{"type":"Hatred","kind":"Ex","details":"A kithangian gains a +2 bonus on all attack rolls and damage rolls made against all creatures of the animal type. In addition, animals take a -2 penalty on all saving throws against a kithangian's supernatural or spell-like abilities."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Sting-injury; save Fort DC 20; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Str plus nauseated; cure 2 consecutive saves."},{"type":"Rasping Tongues","kind":"Su","details":"The faces between a kithangian's claws have long rasping tongues covered with tiny teeth. Whenever a kithangian successfully grapples a foe with its claws, a rasping tongue slithers out from the face within and burrows into the creature's body. Each round that the creature is grappled, it takes 1d6 points of damage and 1d4 points of Charisma damage as its sense of self-identity is warped and twisted. A successful DC 18 Will save negates the Charisma damage. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Swift Transformation","kind":"Su","details":"A kithangian can use its change shape ability as a swift action."}],"description":"Kithangians, also known as beast demons, are reprehensible monstrosities born from the souls of those who abused and tormented animals in life. Universally male, the sudden spread of fiendish elements through within an area's fauna is a sure indication of a kithangian's presence in a region. The fact that most creatures that birth litters of young with the half-fiendish template die in the process is of little concern to the kithangian, for it merely moves on to new hunting grounds when uncorrupted animal victims grow too rare.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Lava Drake","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d12+44","hdvalue":11,"fort":11,"ref":10,"will":8,"immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":30,"special":"lava only"},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"bite +17 (1d8+7), 2 claws +17 (1d6+7), tail slap +15 (1d8+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"magma shake"},{"type":"pyroclastic vomit"}],"strength":25,"dexterity":16,"constitution":18,"intelligence":9,"wisdom":12,"charisma":11,"baseatk":11,"cmb":19,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":32,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":21},{"skill":"Fly","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13,"special":"+21 submerged in molten rock or metal"}],"languages":["Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"hold breath"},{"type":"speed surge"}],"environments":["any hills","any mountains","warm forests"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","rampage (3-12)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This muscular two-legged dragon is covered with scales of thick volcanic stone.","group":"Drake","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Magma Shake","kind":"Ex","details":"Whenever a lava drake exits from being submerged in molten rock (either magma or lava), on the next round as a full-round action, it can shake its body, flicking a fine spray of scalding molten rock in every direction. All creatures within a 30-foot radius of the lava drake take 5d6 points of fire damage from the shower of scalding rock; a successful DC 18 Reflex save halves the damage. Performing a magma shake clears the drake's scales of all excess molten rock and it must resubmerge itself in order to use this attack again. The save DC is Dexterity-based."},{"type":"Pyroclastic Vomit","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a lava drake can vomit forth a ball of molten rock that explodes upon striking a target, showering the target and adjacent creatures in magma. This attack has a range of 100 ft., and deals 6d6 points of fire damage (Reflex DC 19 half) to the primary target and 3d6 points of fire damage to any creatures within 20 ft. of the primary target. The magma continues to burn for 1d3 rounds, dealing an additional 3d6 points of fire damage per round to the primary target and 1d6 points of fire damage per round to any secondary targets. After the magma cools, it crumbles to dust. Once a lava drake has used its pyroclastic vomit, it cannot do so again for 1d6 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Speed Surge","kind":"Ex","details":"Three times per day as a swift action, a lava drake can draw on its draconic heritage for a boost of strength and speed that allows it to take an addition move action that round."}],"description":"The deviant and destructive cousins of primal magma dragons, lava drakes rise from smoldering volcanic crevasses to terrorize and devour those creatures weaker than themselves. While far less intelligent that their draconic kin, they are equally arrogant and seek out the adoration of humanoids. They can and often do submerge themselves in molten rock, burrowing through the lava to sneak up on prey, or to provide a dramatic display of power to those who worship them. Thick, black-crusted scales cover a lava drake's body. Stockier than other drakes, adults can grow up to 18 ft. in length and weigh over 3,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Lava Lurker","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","fire"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +11 natural","hp":114,"hd":"12d10+48","hdvalue":12,"fort":12,"ref":9,"will":4,"immunities":["electricity","elemental traits","fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold","vulnerable to water"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"swim","speed":30,"special":"in molten rock only"}],"melee":"2 slams +20 (1d6+8 plus burn)","ranged":"magma ball +14 (1d6+8 plus burn)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"1d6 fire, DC 20"},{"type":"death throes"}],"strength":26,"dexterity":13,"constitution":18,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":10,"charisma":11,"baseatk":12,"cmb":20,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deadly Aim"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Stand Still"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (magma ball)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16,"special":"+20 in magma"},{"skill":"Swim","value":31}],"languages":["Ignan"],"environments":["any underground","any mountains (volcano)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","flow (3-6)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"Spatters of magma sear everything that comes near this vaguely humanoid mass of endlessly melting and reforming rock.","source":"The Emerald Spire","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Throes","kind":"Ex","details":"When a lava lurker is slain, its body implodes, creating an extinguishing vacuum. All creatures within a 5-foot-radius burst take 8d6 points of cold damage (Reflex DC 20 half). In addition to the damage, every affected square is targeted by quench (CL 10th). This also targets all fire effects and magic items that create and control flame. If the lava lurker is killed in a pool of magma, it solidifies the rock within the area of effect, though in an active magma flow or similar natural and nearly endless s."},{"type":"Vulnerable to Water","kind":"Ex","details":"If a significant amount of water- such as the contents of a large bucket, the liquid created by a create water spell, or a blow from a water elemental- strikes a lava lurker, the lava lurker must succeed at a DC 20 Fortitude save or be staggered for 2d4 rounds. A lava lurker that is immersed in water is automatically staggered and must succeed at a DC 20 Fortitude save each round or be petrified (this DC increases by 1 on each subsequent round), reverting to its molten stone form once the water is gone."}],"description":"Territorial swimmers through the molten veins that crisscross the hottest depths of mortal worlds and the Elemental Plane of Earth, lava lurkers claim active magma flows and the fiery lakes within smoldering volcanoes as their homes. Most are content to stay within such burning depths, threatening only those foolish enough to wander close to such obviously deadly natural hazards. But occasionally, during volcanic eruptions or other explosive geological events, lava lurkers are forced from their comfortable homes, becoming unwilling riders on blazing rapids. While these disasters rarely threaten lava lurkers' elemental forms, they do often force the creatures into-or worse, strand them in-areas they find uncomfortably cool.\n\nDull-witted lava lurkers eagerly sow fires and throw magma as they wander semi-aimlessly, doing what they can to create more comfortable surroundings or seeking other nearby warm places-like furnaces or bonfires-as they try to find their way back to active volcanic flows. They care little for non-elemental creatures, being baffled and annoyed by the shrill noises such creatures make when they're exposed to even the slightest fleck of molten rock.\n\nThough lava lurkers live in earth and flame, they die with a chilling inward gasp. If slain, the final surge of a lava lurker's animating fires consumes the nearby air, creating a momentary vacuum that extinguishes surrounding flames. This instantly transforms a lava lurker's body into a perfectly cool hunk of rock and often quells lesser flames nearby, if only temporarily.\n\nupply of molten rock, cooled rock might melt again after only a few moments. The save DC is Constitution-based.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Leanan Sidhe","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"fey","subtypes":["mythic"],"init":7,"init_special":"mythic","senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+5 deflection, +3 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 natural","hp":100,"hd":"11d6+62","hdvalue":11,"fort":12,"ref":15,"will":13,"dr":"10/cold iron and epic","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":30,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"dagger +5 (1d4/19-20) or touch +5 (1d4 Cha damage)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"life drain"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"3/day, surge +1d6"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"calm emotions"},{"spell":"crushing despair"},{"spell":"dimension door","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"animal trance"},{"spell":"quickened charm person"}]}],"strength":10,"dexterity":17,"constitution":18,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":12,"charisma":21,"baseatk":5,"cmb":5,"cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Persuasive","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (charm person)"},{"feat":"Spell Focus (enchantment)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":19},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":25},{"skill":"Fly","value":7},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":7},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":19},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":6}],"languages":["Sylvan","tongues"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"any female humanoid"},{"type":"skill blessing"},{"type":"spell blessing"},{"type":"unearthly grace"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary","retinue (1 plus 3-7 guards and sycophants of 1st-3rd level)"],"treasure":"double (dagger)","description_visual":"This serene woman has pointed ears and flowing crimson hair, and wears an elegant dress and a crown of twigs.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Life Drain","kind":"Ex","details":"A leanan sidhe immediately knows if a creature uses her skill blessing or spell blessing. As a standard action at any range, she can expend one use of mythic power to drain 1 point of Constitution from that creature. The leanan sidhe heals 5 hit points or gains 5 temporary hit points for 1 hour (up to a maximum number of temporary hit points equal to her full normal hit points) each time she uses this ability."},{"type":"Skill Blessing","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a leanan sidhe can create a special token that takes the form of a masterwork artisan's tool for one Craft or Perform skill. The intended recipient of this tool gains a +4 bonus on skill checks made with the token. Like with a cursed item, the recipient prefers to use the token, refuses to get rid of it, and finds that it returns if stolen or discarded. The leanan sidhe can destroy the token as a standard action at any range. She can have a number of tokens in existence equal to her mythic rank."},{"type":"Spell Blessing","kind":"Su","details":"A leanan sidhe may enhance the magic of a willing humanoid spellcaster by touching him for 1 full round. The blessing allows the target to recall a number of spell levels each day equal to twice the leanan sidhe's mythic rank. This recalling works like a pearl of power, except it works for spellcasters of any class (spontaneous casters recover spent spell slots). The leanan sidhe can end this blessing as a standard action at any range. The number of blessed creatures she can have at the same time is equal to her mythic rank."},{"type":"Unearthly Grace","kind":"Su","details":"A leanan sidhe adds her Charisma modifier as a racial bonus on all her saving throws and as a deflection bonus to her AC."}],"description":"Leanan sidhe are regal fey who pride themselves as patrons of the arts. By establishing a magical link with a talented mortal performer or artist, the leanan sidhe enhances her target's skill, but slowly feeds on his life energy. Many tragic stories of talented artists who have a creative burst and then fall into obscurity or suddenly die can be attributed to the inf luence of these creatures. A leanan sidhe prefers to avoid direct combat and relies on her minions and devotees to protect her-all of whom hope to become her next special project, despite the cost of this arrangement.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Leukodaemon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["daemon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"deathwatch"},{"type":"detect good"}],"auras":["infectious aura (50 ft.)"],"ac":23,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+7 Dex, +7 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"10d10+60","hdvalue":10,"fort":9,"ref":14,"will":12,"dr":"10/good or silver","immunities":["acid","death effects","disease","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":20,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"bite +16 (1d8+7), 2 claws +16 (1d6+7)","ranged":"+1 composite longbow +18 (2d6+8/x3 plus contagion)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath of flies"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"deathwatch"},{"spell":"detect good"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"contagion"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"harm"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 3, 1 leukodaemon only, 35%"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":24,"constitution":23,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":21,"charisma":16,"baseatk":10,"cmb":18,"cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Point- Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (longbow)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Heal","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16},{"skill":"Survival","value":15},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":16}],"languages":["Abyssal","Draconic","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abaddon)"],"organizations":["solitary","wake (2-10)"],"treasure":"standard (+1 composite longbow)","description_visual":"This human-shaped beast has a horse's skull for a head. It walks on cracked hooves and bears the rotting wings of a carrion bird.","group":"Daemon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath of Flies","kind":"Su","details":"Once per minute as a standard action, a leukodaemon can unleash a cloud of corpse-bloated, biting black flies in a 20-foot cone. Those caught in the cone take 8d6 points of slashing damage. A DC 21 Reflex save halves this damage. Those who take any damage are also sickened for 1 minute. In addition, the flies linger for 1d4+1 rounds, congealing into a buzzing 20-foot-square cloud centered on the cone's original point of origin. Any creature that ends its turn in this cloud must make a DC 21 Reflex save to avoid taking 4d6 points of damage and becoming sickened for 1 minute. This cloud of flies may be dispersed by any area effect that does damage or creates wind of at least strong wind force. All daemons are immune to this effect. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Contagion","kind":"Su","details":"Any arrow a leukodaemon fires from a bow is tainted with disease. If a creature is damaged by a leukodaemon's arrow, it must make a DC 19 Fortitude save or be affected as if by the spell contagion. A leukodaemon can manifest arrows at will and never runs out of ammunition."},{"type":"Infectious Aura","kind":"Su","details":"All creatures within 50 ft. of a leukodaemon take a -4 penalty on Fortitude saves against disease effects."}],"description":"Deacons of the Horseman of Pestilence, leukodaemons serve their lord in Abaddon as well as across the planes by spreading plagues and pandemics.\n\nLeukodaemons stand upward of 14 ft. tall but weigh just over 200 pounds. The skulls that serve as their heads can be replaced with any skulls, yet these creatures choose horse skulls to show their loyalty to the Horsemen. The creature's true head is merely a blistered knob between its shoulders.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
